## Intended closing lemma

Couple retained physical crossings, deleted/interface crossings and virtual
inter-grain determinant mass to the *actual* shell residual, or construct a
same-cardinality competitor strictly below the source diameter.

`joint source-level transfer -> G+E >= (sqrt(3)/4)B +
(sqrt(3)/2)(t+chi-1) -> contradict Section 36's strict global upper side`.

This closes Target B only if its topology/flexible-branch hypotheses are
also covered; it is not automatically a Level I proof.

## Mechanisms under attack

1. Static determinant payment with roundness and the strict n-1 comparison.
   Test whether these extra global necessary conditions repair the known
   far-from-optimal two-grain regression.
2. Common phase-offset contraction. Check every cross-grain source pair,
   including actual diameters, rather than only rhombus areas.
3. Whole-source lattice replacement. Compare a finite perturbed source to
   its unperturbed triangular-lattice packing at identical cardinality.

The first candidate to falsify is:
`M_inter <= C(G+E+B+|t+chi-1|)` for a universal C on near-disk,
unit-separated sources satisfying the strict n-1 comparison. If false,
the missing bridge is genuine global optimality/rigidity, not merely those
scalar necessary conditions.

All resulting claims remain noncanonical pending independent scrutiny.
